{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542774-harrowed-wolves-a-homebrew-mage-werewolf-hybrid-template","id":1542774,"title":"Harrowed Wolves: A Homebrew Mage-Werewolf Hybrid Template","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-27T08:23:37-07:00","id":1542774,"title":"Harrowed Wolves: A Homebrew Mage-Werewolf Hybrid Template","content":"This is a general concept I've continually circled back to over the years: namely, throwing Mage and Werewolf into a blender to create a horrifying smoothy of angst. The following seems the most narratively and mechanically satisfying implementation I've come up with, and I figured, why not share my misguided genius?<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harrowed Wolves</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Under an unusual confluence of cosmic variables and perhaps conflicting divine wills, a Wolf-Blooded may begin the road to Awakening, only to have their First Change thrust upon them while at the cusp of imprinting their name upon a Watchtower. This isn\u2019t </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>entirely </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">as implausible as it sounds; the experiences leading up a First Change can certainly fulfill the \u201cconfrontation with the supernatural\u201d prerequisite for Awakening. In any case, the result is an aborted Awakening, with all that entails. But as if that weren\u2019t bad enough, the multiplicative strain of both supernatural forces warring over the unfortunate\u2019s soul prevents the new Uratha\u2019s Harmony from developing properly. This so-called Harrowed Wolf finds themselves caught between their malformed Gnosis and their half-spirit nature, barely held together by the tattered threads of their humanity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harrowed Wolf Characters</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harrowed Wolves mechanically possess both the Harrowed Banisher template (Nameless and Accursed pg. 52) and Forsaken template (Werewolf: the Forsaken Core 2e pg 82, unless you really want to make a Pure instead), with some modification.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity replaces both Wisdom and Harmony. This has the usual effects described for Harrowed Banishers, though with different consequences for breaking points (see below). Replacing Harmony with Integrity works as follows:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conditions that normally trigger breaking points towards Flesh or Spirit instead trigger an Integrity breaking point. Treat the Harrowed Wolf\u2019s Harmony as 5 for determining what triggers a breaking point, and for determining the bonus/penalty to the Resolve+Composure roll (i.e. no modifier by default). For all other purposes (e.g. shapeshifting costs, length of control during </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Wasu-Im</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, etc.), treat the Harrowed Wolf\u2019s Harmony as 8. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The possible outcomes of Integrity breaking points differ from normal: in place of the usual Condition on a success or failure, the Harrowed Wolf enters </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Wasu-Im</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, as if they\u2019d experienced a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kuruth </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">trigger. They immediately enter </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Basu-Im</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> on a dramatic failure. Failure or dramatic failure both still cause a dot of Integrity loss. Exceptional success grants a beat and point of willpower as normal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harrowed Wolves still suffer from general </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Kuruth</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> triggers, but don\u2019t have an additional personal trigger. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural Tolerance and Potency</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harrowed Wolves possess both Gnosis and Primal Urge. Use the usual listed trait to calculate die pools for power-activation or Clash of Wills, (e.g. Gnosis for casting spells, Primal Urge for Gifts). Use the higher of the two scores as the Harrowed Wolf\u2019s Supernatural Tolerance when resisting or contesting hostile effects.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of separate mana and essence pools, the Harrowed Wolf possesses a single resource pool, which can contain points of Mana and Essence in any combination, up to a limit determined by the higher of the maximum mana or essence determined by their Gnosis/Primal Urge. Their limit on spending either resource per turn is determined separately by the corresponding trait. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All other benefits and drawbacks of the two traits apply normally. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anchors</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harrowed Wolves possess a Blood and Bone and Touchstones, rather than a Virtue or Vice. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Creating a Harrowed Wolf</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When creating a Harrowed Wolf as a player character, follow the Newly Awakened template to determine starting Arcana ratings, merits, etc. When applying the Forsaken template, only select a single Shadow Gift. A Harrowed Wolf\u2019s starting Integrity is 6.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> This is mainly a theory-crafting exercise; I'd be surprised if it ever sees actual use in-play. But I'll accept feedback, regardless.<br /> <br /> (The main part I'm not entirely satisfied with is the semi-arbitrary effective Harmony ratings. But most other implementations I toyed with strayed a bit too close to &quot;Harmony with extra steps&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T11:23:07-07:00","id":1542786,"title":"","content":"I like the general concept, though would they not be more likely to become rapt than a banisher? Like, <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> already has a mage who turned herself into a spirit hybrid, and the result was she became enraptured.<br /> <br /> Also, for where they come from, I'd wonder if perhaps Luna or the lingering influence of Father Wolf just does that to mages sometimes. Like, the Watchtowers won't Awaken supernatural creatures, but I don't remember anything being said about the other way around? Maybe if a Thyrsus spends too long in the Shadow there's a risk they become 'infected' with the influence of Moon or Wolf.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, that last one might be quite good as a reinforcement of the idea that mages of whatever power, are ultimately always outsiders to the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T15:03:16-07:00","id":1542802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542774-harrowed-wolves-a-homebrew-mage-werewolf-hybrid-template?p=1542786#post1542786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the general concept, though would they not be more likely to become rapt than a banisher? Like, <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> already has a mage who turned herself into a spirit hybrid, and the result was she became enraptured.<br /> <br /> Also, for where they come from, I'd wonder if perhaps Luna or the lingering influence of Father Wolf just does that to mages sometimes. Like, the Watchtowers won't Awaken supernatural creatures, but I don't remember anything being said about the other way around? Maybe if a Thyrsus spends too long in the Shadow there's a risk they become 'infected' with the influence of Moon or Wolf.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, that last one might be quite good as a reinforcement of the idea that mages of whatever power, are ultimately always outsiders to the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Convention seems to be that Awakening puts you outside the purview of most other big forces. As of Signs of Sorcery, Awakening even de-wolf-bloods you. But I'm not in a position to decry weird edge cases, so I wouldn't rule out <i>something</i> happening if a low-Wisdom mage pokes the wrong Lune with a stick for too long.<br /> <br /> In any case, Rapt implies a descent into un-Wise tomfoolery after already having been a mage*, so it's coming at the concept from a different angle than what I was going for.<br /> <br /> *I'm just now remembering an NPC I had immediately go Rapt upon Awakening. I forget exactly why. Probably had to do with the fact that a Seer was puppeteering him at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T22:34:39-07:00","id":1542809,"title":"","content":"Running down a quick list of practical/thematic questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are a Harrowed Wolf's Blood and Bone subject to potential shifting as they raise their Gnosis like normal mages?<br /> 2. What determines whether a Harrowed Wolf's physical and spiritual Touchstones are still attached?<br /> 3. Does the fixed effective Harmony rating of 8 for a Harrowed Wolf mean they are always capable of Reaching to enter the physical world from the Shadow without a locus?<br /> 4. Is there any difference in how a Harrowed Wolf's Peripheral Mage Sight penalizes their actions to account for their shapeshifting and spirit senses giving them more supernatural distractions that are on the one hand their own powers but on the other hand non-Supernal phenomena?<br /> 5. Are there any constraints on the Path and/or Auspice of a Harrowed Wolf?<br /> 6. Are Harrowed Wolves incapable of joining a Tribe like some of the Ghost Wolf-specific oddities in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-28T02:42:11-07:00","id":1542811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542774-harrowed-wolves-a-homebrew-mage-werewolf-hybrid-template?p=1542802#post1542802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Convention seems to be that Awakening puts you outside the purview of most other big forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my point. <i>Awakening</i> does that (or more accurately, the Watchtowers just won't bother with you otherwise), but that doesn't much protect you further down the line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm not in a position to decry weird edge cases, so I wouldn't rule out <i>something</i> happening if a low-Wisdom mage pokes the wrong Lune with a stick for too long. </div> </div> </div>That's kinda my thinking. Though, low wisdom isn't necessarily important to becoming enraptured. It's explicit that you can be enraptured simply by circumstance. Get on the wrong side of some cosmic force and it'll rip the wisdom right out of you in one go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, Rapt implies a descent into un-Wise tomfoolery after already having been a mage*, so it's coming at the concept from a different angle than what I was going for. </div> </div> </div>There is a character in <i>N&amp;A</i> who became enraptured at the point she awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T13:35:58-07:00","id":1542930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1542774-harrowed-wolves-a-homebrew-mage-werewolf-hybrid-template?p=1542809#post1542809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running down a quick list of practical/thematic questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are a Harrowed Wolf's Blood and Bone subject to potential shifting as they raise their Gnosis like normal mages?<br /> 2. What determines whether a Harrowed Wolf's physical and spiritual Touchstones are still attached?<br /> 3. Does the fixed effective Harmony rating of 8 for a Harrowed Wolf mean they are always capable of Reaching to enter the physical world from the Shadow without a locus?<br /> 4. Is there any difference in how a Harrowed Wolf's Peripheral Mage Sight penalizes their actions to account for their shapeshifting and spirit senses giving them more supernatural distractions that are on the one hand their own powers but on the other hand non-Supernal phenomena?<br /> 5. Are there any constraints on the Path and/or Auspice of a Harrowed Wolf?<br /> 6. Are Harrowed Wolves incapable of joining a Tribe like some of the Ghost Wolf-specific oddities in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I suppose, yeah.<br /> 2. I'll be honest, I kinda forgot about Touchstones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Strictly as I wrote the rules, a Harrowed Wolf can just never benefit from a spiritual Touchstone (though, again, the effective Harmony thing isn't something I'm <i>100%</i> happy with).<br /> 3. Indeed (see above mild dissatisfaction with Harmony).<br /> 4. Good question. I intended that their non-Mage abilities just count as non-Supernal. You could make an argument that it should be -2 I suppose. But part of me always wanted to flip the penalties of &quot;own&quot; versus &quot;other&quot; powers anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 5. None. The idea is more that the Awakening and Change are independent and in conflict with each other*, rather than some merging that would require them to be Thyrsus Ithaeur or whatever. (*Unless they achieve nirvana and become a Pangeaen or something).<br /> 6. I had considered this. It makes a fair bit of sense; the link to a Watchtower taking up the space a link to a Firstborn might. I lean slightly towards &quot;yes&quot;. With maybe a story hook that successfully joining a Tribe might be a way to reboot their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 09-30-2024, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}